# GLM-5.3-Flash W4A16 on 4 CUDA GPUs (sm_80 Ampere patches)
# Copy to .env and edit. ./start.sh does this for you on first run.
# Every setting below is commented out and shows the default the scripts use
# when it is unset, so a later release's new defaults reach you on
# ./start.sh update without editing .env. Uncomment a line to override that
# default; delete or re-comment it to go back to the default. The paths
# (/path/to/...), HF_TOKEN and TORCH_INDEX_URL lines are placeholders, not
# defaults; the note above each says what the default is.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, notes on their own lines starting with #.
# An unquoted value ends at the first " #" (whitespace then #), and a trailing
# "  (...)" (two or more spaces, then a note in parentheses) is dropped too, so
# a note left on the line does not end up in the value. A # or ( that is part
# of the value (a#b, f(x)) is kept. Quote the value, "..." or '...', to keep
# everything between the quotes exactly as written.
# A prefix env assignment overrides this file for every key, including an
# explicit empty (KEY= ./start.sh):   MAX_LEN=131072 ./start.sh restart

# --- engine pin --------------------------------------------------------
# The vLLM fork and the commit it is pinned to. Left commented so a `git pull`
# of this repo can move the pin; ./start.sh reinstalls when it changes.
# Uncomment to freeze the engine. To roll back, set an older pin here (1.2.0
# used 434dea1a1b, 1.1.x 69c33802d0) and run ./start.sh update. A prefix
# assignment (VLLM_COMMIT=<sha> ./start.sh update) lasts for that run only:
# the next plain start or restart reinstalls the default pin.
# VLLM_COMMIT=3bbb99a534
# VLLM_REPO=https://github.com/Morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx.git
# VLLM_BRANCH=ampere-glm53

# --- paths -------------------------------------------------------------
# All default to directories inside this repo (shown below). To move one,
# uncomment it and give an ABSOLUTE path: a relative path is taken from the
# directory you run ./start.sh from, not from this repo.
# Default: venv/ in this repo.
# VENV=/path/to/venv
# Default: vllm-src/ in this repo.
# VLLM_SRC=/path/to/vllm-src
# Default: models/ in this repo.
# MODELS_DIR=/path/to/models
# Default: MODELS_DIR/GLM-5.3-Flash-W4A16-MTP.
# MODEL=/path/to/GLM-5.3-Flash-W4A16-MTP
# Default: MODELS_DIR/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2.
# DFLASH_MODEL=/path/to/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2
# CUDA toolkit root. Triton and TileLang JIT against it at runtime.
# CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-13.3

# --- weights -----------------------------------------------------------
# TARGET_REPO=canada-quant/GLM-5.3-Flash-W4A16-MTP
# DRAFTER_REPO=incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2
# Unauthenticated Hub downloads are rate limited; a token is faster.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# 1 re-fetches the weights even when the files are already there.
# REFRESH_WEIGHTS=0

# --- API ---------------------------------------------------------------
# 127.0.0.1 = reachable from this machine only. To serve other machines, set
# HOST to 0.0.0.0 (every interface) or one of this machine's addresses, and set
# API_KEY first: without it anyone who can reach the port can use the model.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8000
# When set, every /v1 request must send "Authorization: Bearer <key>".
# ./start.sh smoke and status send it for you. Unset = no key.
# API_KEY=
# SERVED_MODEL_NAME=glm-5.3-flash
# Parsers for GLM-5.3's reasoning blocks and tool calls.
# REASONING_PARSER=glm47
# TOOL_PARSER=glm47

# --- layout ------------------------------------------------------------
# PP * TP must equal the number of GPUs (4).
#
# Tensor parallel over all four cards (TP=4) is the layout this release
# supports and what every number in the README was measured with. It assumes
# PCIe Gen2 x16 links between the cards:
# tensor parallelism moves about 9.4 MB per layer during prefill and roughly
# 100 small collectives per decode step, so on stock x4 links it is bus-bound
# and far slower than the published figures.
#
# PP is left as a knob because the engine supports it, but PP=4 is
# UNSUPPORTED IN THIS RELEASE: nothing here is tuned for it. A
# pipeline-parallel layout for narrower links is planned for a later release.
# PP=1
# TP=4
# Layer split under PP only. Empty uses the balanced default for the mode.
# VLLM_PP_LAYER_PARTITION=

# --- engine sizing -----------------------------------------------------
# Context ceiling. With this release's defaults, 262144 gives a 1,174,567-token
# KV pool at GPU_UTIL 0.95, 4.48x concurrency at full context (1,187,776 and
# 4.53x with the optional peer-to-peer path on). Raising it lowers that.
# MAX_LEN=262144
# Concurrent sequences.
# MAX_SEQS=8
# Batched tokens per scheduler step; this sets the prefill chunk size:
# chunk = floor((MAX_BATCHED - SPEC_N) / 1152) x 1152. The default 3460 gives
# 3,456-token chunks (+2.4% cold prefill against 2,304-token chunks at 180 W
# per card, for about 35,600 fewer KV tokens).
# 2048 gives 1.2.0's 1,152-token chunks.
# MAX_BATCHED=3460
# Fraction of each GPU vLLM may use. 0.95 is what we run; 0.97 was too tight.
# GPU_UTIL=0.95

# --- speculative decoding ----------------------------------------------
# dflash = the DFlash2 drafter (needs DRAFTER_REPO downloaded)
# mtp    = the MTP head inside the target checkpoint
# none   = no speculation
# Unset, TP=4 uses dflash. Uncomment to force one.
# SPEC_MODE=dflash
# Draft tokens per step. k=3 is what the README numbers use.
# SPEC_N=3

# --- prefill -----------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream's UNCONDITIONAL long-prefill chunk cap. LEAVE IT 0. It cost -15.3%
# prefill and +16.5% time to first token on a 23K prompt here, and it silently disables the prefill
# overlap and the prefill kernels by dropping chunks below their gates.
# PREFILL_CAP=0
# Decode-aware chunking: the cap that only applies while something is decoding.
# This is the one you want. 0 turns it off.
# FAIR_PREFILL=1
# FAIR_CHUNK=384
# FAIR_PARTIAL=2

# --- sm_80 feature flags (kill switches) -------------------------------
# All of these are OFF by default in the engine code; serve.sh is the only thing
# that turns them on, so each is a one-variable kill switch. Uncomment one with 0 and
# restart — no rebuild, no revert.
#
# If output quality is ever in question, try VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_KERNELS=0 first.
#
# TP prefill comm/compute overlap (TP>1 only; on by default under TP=4).
# VLLM_GLM5_PREFILL_OVERLAP=1
# VLLM_GLM5_PREFILL_OVERLAP_SPLITS=2
# sm_80 prefill kernels: mHC pre-norm projection + sparse-MLA DSA attention.
# VLLM_GLM5_PREFILL_KERNELS=1
# Chunk-size gate for those kernels. 384, not the code default 512, because
# FAIR_CHUNK caps the chunk at 384 while something decodes.
# VLLM_GLM5_PREFILL_MIN_TOKENS=384
# Fused eager decode prologue.
# VLLM_GLM5_PROLOGUE_FUSE=1
# Batch-sharded logits and sampling (TP>1 only; on by default under TP=4).
# VLLM_GLM5_LOCAL_LOGITS=1
# sm_80 decode kernels: fused mHC post+pre, MoE routing/align, KDA decode.
# VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_KERNELS=1
# sm_80 thin-M BF16 GEMM for the linears W4A16 leaves unquantized.
# VLLM_GLM5_THIN_GEMM=1
# Host-staged all-reduce for nodes without GPU peer access (TP>1 only; on by
# default under TP=4).
# VLLM_GLM5_HOST_ALLREDUCE=1
# Submit the MoE shared experts after the routed dispatch so the two overlap
# on the aux stream. Decode only. 0 restores the upstream ordering.
# VLLM_GLM5_SHARED_EXPERT_REORDER=1

# More switches. Each line shows the default serve.sh sets; uncomment it
# with 0 to switch that one off.
#
# Second-generation decode kernels (TP only; on by default under TP=4).
# Indexer decode glue folded into fewer kernels.
# VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_IDX_GLUE=1
# KDA decode, gate projections fused.
# VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_KDA_V2=1
# MoE gate + top-k + align in one kernel.
# VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_MOE_ROUTE_V2=1
# mHC decode v2.
# VLLM_GLM5_DECODE_MHC_V2=1
# Drafter RoPE cache sized to the context: more KV.
# VLLM_GLM5_DRAFTER_ROPE_FIT=1
#
# Repeatable output: the same request on its own gives the same output every
# time (on by default).
# MoE block alignment in a fixed order.
# VLLM_GLM5_DETERMINISTIC_MOE_ALIGN=1
# CUDA-graph padding rows kept out of the MoE.
# VLLM_GLM5_MOE_MASK_PADDING=1
# Indexer top-k consistent on exact ties.
# VLLM_GLM5_TOPK_TIEFIX=1
# Indexer top-k returned in a fixed order.
# VLLM_GLM5_TOPK_SORTED=1
# Small batches: the above split across more programs.
# VLLM_GLM5_TOPK_TIEFIX_SPLIT_ROWS=8
#
# KV headroom (TP only; on by default under TP=4). Outputs are bit-identical.
# Prefill indexer logits budget; 512 = off.
# VLLM_SPARSE_INDEXER_MAX_LOGITS_MB=128
# Drafter selector tables split across the cards.
# VLLM_GLM5_DRAFTER_SELECTOR_SHARD=1
# Indexer decode tables sized by decode rows.
# VLLM_GLM5_INDEXER_DECODE_ROWS=1
# Indexer gather workspace clamp (engine default).
# VLLM_GLM5_INDEXER_GATHER_CLAMP=1
#
# Sparse-attention decode schedule. The retuned one (1.2.0 on) is on in the
# engine; 1 brings back the older schedule.
# VLLM_GLM5_SPARSE_MLA_DECODE_LEGACY=0

# --- optional: PCIe peer-to-peer ---------------------------------------
# Device-memory CustomAllreduce over PCIe peer-to-peer instead of staging
# every collective through the host. OFF here, because peer-to-peer has to be
# available at the driver level first -- `nvidia-smi topo -p2p r` must report
# OK rather than GNS. See "PCIe peer-to-peer (optional)" in the README.
# On this release: decode step -3.7% at one user, -6.9% at four, -8.3% at six,
# -6.2% at eight, cold prefill unchanged, and 13,209 more KV tokens.
# VLLM_ALLOW_PCIE_P2P_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE=0
# Which CustomAllreduce kernel. 2stage, because the built-in crossover is
# NVLink-tuned and wrong on Gen2 x16. Inert unless the switch above is 1.
# VLLM_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE_ALGO=2stage
# The switch also picks the caching allocator, because CustomAllreduce needs
# legacy CUDA IPC handles that the expandable_segments (VMM) allocator cannot
# provide. Set PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF explicitly only if you mean to override
# that; an explicit value wins over the switch's choice.
# PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=

# --- other ------------------------------------------------------------
# Replicated input-embedding table under TP: saves 2 all-reduces per step for
# +0.74 GiB per rank (-6% KV tokens). Off — the KV is worth more here.
# VLLM_GLM5_REPLICATED_EMBED=0

# --- multimodal --------------------------------------------------------
# 0 leaves vision and video uncapped, which makes the memory profiler reserve
# for a context-filling video and costs roughly 150k KV tokens.
# 1 bounds both the profiler dummy and real inputs to the values below.
# MM_CAP=0
# MM_IMAGES=4
# MM_FRAMES=32
# MM_MAX_PIXELS=1003520

# --- lifecycle ---------------------------------------------------------
# Seconds ./start.sh waits for /health. Weight load plus CUDA-graph capture on
# a 320B MoE is slow.
# READY_TIMEOUT=1800
# Seconds ./start.sh stop waits after SIGINT before SIGKILL.
# STOP_TIMEOUT=120
# Preflight thresholds. MIN_GPUS should match PP*TP. The preflight stops,
# before any download, if a card reports less than MIN_GPU_MIB (60 GiB).
# NEED_DISK_GB is in GiB (the checkpoints take ~180 GiB).
# MIN_GPUS=4
# MIN_GPU_MIB=61440
# NEED_DISK_GB=185

# --- build -------------------------------------------------------------
# 0 installs upstream's precompiled extensions (minutes). The patches touch no
# CUDA or C++ source, so they are the same objects you would compile, and they
# already carry sm_80 cubins.
# 1 compiles them yourself: needs the full toolkit, ~60 GB scratch, 1-2 hours.
# BUILD_FROM_SOURCE=0
# MAX_JOBS=16
# TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=8.0
# Only if torch does not resolve to a CUDA build on your platform. PyPI's
# linux torch 2.13.0 is already the cu130 build.
# TORCH_INDEX_URL=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130

# --- extra -------------------------------------------------------------
# Appended verbatim to the vllm serve command line. A --speculative-config
# here wins and no second one is added.
# EXTRA_ARGS=
